====================================================================================================================
2. Voice models fetched into the core image at build time
====================================================================================================================

core/Dockerfile downloads these files once, each checked against a pinned SHA-256 (core/pisa/connectors/
voice_models.py). They are not in this repository.

3D-Speaker CAM++ speaker embedding (3dspeaker_speech_campplus_sv_en_voxceleb_16k.onnx)
  Apache-2.0 (3D-Speaker); trained on VoxCeleb, licensed CC BY 4.0.
WeSpeaker ResNet34 speaker embedding (wespeaker_en_voxceleb_resnet34_LM.onnx)
  Apache-2.0 (WeSpeaker code); the weights follow VoxCeleb, licensed CC BY 4.0.
  VoxCeleb: the University of Oxford Visual Geometry Group (https://www.robots.ox.ac.uk/~vgg/data/voxceleb/).
Silero VAD v4 (silero_vad.onnx)
  MIT, by the Silero team (https://github.com/snakers4/silero-vad).
Smart Turn v3.2 (smart-turn-v3.2-cpu.onnx)
  BSD-2-Clause, by Daily (https://github.com/pipecat-ai/smart-turn).
The files are served from the sherpa-onnx project's releases (Apache-2.0, https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx)
and from Hugging Face (pipecat-ai/smart-turn-v3).

====================================================================================================================
3. Public data
====================================================================================================================

The files in core/tests/data/public/ are synthetic: invented content in each public source's file format (their
README). No data from the sources is in this repository.

At run time PISA reads public feeds and shows each one's credit line with what it used (core/pisa/domain/
public_sources.py), as their licences ask: Roma Servizi per la Mobilità (CC BY-SA 4.0), the MTA (its developer
terms), the Dipartimento della Protezione Civile (CC BY 4.0), Regione Lazio (IODL 2.0), NOAA / National Weather
Service (US public domain), Open-Meteo (CC BY 4.0).

Product and organisation names above belong to their owners and are used only to identify their works.
